# Sample Dialer entries for Popular High-Speed and Generic Hayes Modems## Dialer  - dialer seqences# &Dialer - hangup seqences for the device# @Dialer - strings that will abort the dial#           (these strings are only looked for after \T is used)## Practical Paripherals PM9600SA with the following defaults# AT &F &C1 &D3 S0=1 E0 L0 T Q2 &W# PM9600SA No Error-correction, no cpmpressionPPI96 "" AT OK-AT-OK AT&Q6S7=120S2=43S95=44 OK ATDT\T CONNECT&PPI96 "" +++\d\d\c OK-AT-OK ATH@PPI96 BUSY NO\sCARRIER# PM9600SA Auto Error-correction, auto compression &q5PPI384 "" AT OK-AT-OK AT&Q5E0S7=120S2=43S95=44 OK ATDT\T CONNECT&PPI384 "" +++\d\d\c OK-AT-OK ATH@PPI384 BUSY NO\sCARRIER## Telebit TrailBlazer with the following defaults# AT &F S51=254 S52=2 S53=3 S110=1 S111=30 S45=0 Q6 &Wtb1200  "" **A\dA\dA\dAT "" ATS50=2DT\T CONNECT\s1200tb2400  "" **A\dA\dA\dAT "" ATS50=3DT\T CONNECT\s2400tbfast  "" **A\dA\dA\dAT "" ATS50=255DT\T CONNECT\sFAST## Standard Hayes 2400 baud modemHAYES  "" AT OK ATDT\T CONNECT&HAYES  "" +++\d\c OK ATH OK@HAYES BUSY NO\sCARRIER## Direct line - No ModemDirect "" ""&Direct "" ""